# EXPERT (10): integrated, independent scenarios with intermediate checks.
case('Expert','Scheduling end-to-end','R03 R11 R12 R13 R14 R36','Complete booking, staff rescheduling and cancellation with consistent history.', 'F0 P;two valid future slots;independent older cancelled appointment', 'Book first slot as P and inspect Dashboard. | Request reschedule. | As staff move to second slot. | Verify replacement opens immediately. | As P inspect replacement then cancel with new reason. | Inspect history and notifications.', 'Whole scheduling lifecycle remains consistent across roles.', 'Original booking becomes cancelled due to reschedule; replacement has correct slot. | Independent old cancellation is retained. | Replacement opens after staff action. | Final upcoming excludes cancelled replacement. | Reasons, history, dashboard and relevant notifications agree.')
case('Expert','Laboratory end-to-end','R15 R16 R17 R28 R30 R36','Create, publish, correct and withdraw a result across staff and patient views.', 'F0 P with same-test history;authorized staff;unique new test record', 'Staff creates unpublished result. | Patient verifies absence. | Staff publishes. | Patient follows notification, checks details/trend and downloads PDF. | Staff corrects result value/status then patient reopens. | Staff withdraws; patient retries saved links.', 'Publication/correction/withdrawal consistently governs all representations.', 'Unpublished absent; published notified. | Patient/trend/PDF use current corrected value and status after correction. | Withdrawal blocks list/detail/export. | No unsupported diagnosis; unrelated tests unchanged.')
case('Expert','Messaging end-to-end','R18 R19 R36','Exchange messages across roles and verify per-user archive independence.', 'F0 P and Physician;unique subject', 'Patient composes Medical Question. | Physician reads and replies. | Patient follows notification and reads reply. | Patient archives thread. | Physician confirms thread remains accessible. | Patient restores it to Inbox and reopens.', 'Communication and folder/read states are persistent and user-specific.', 'Correct recipients/authors/thread history. | Notification and unread transition accurate. | Patient archive does not archive physician view. | Archive/restore confirmations and destination navigation work. | No message lost/duplicated.')
case('Expert','Refills end-to-end','R20 R21 R36 R40','Resolve a denied refill then process a separate new request to completion.', 'F0 active medicine;no pending refill;authorized staff', 'Patient requests refill with note. | Staff reviews and denies with reason. | Patient reads denial. | Patient submits a distinct new request. | Staff reviews, approves and completes it with final note. | Patient inspects history and notifications.', 'Distinct decisions/history are preserved through the full simulated lifecycle.', 'Denied request stays denied with reason. | New request is separately tracked. | Final request Completed with correct note. | Progress/notifications and refill decision audit match. | No real prescription transmission.')
case('Expert','Billing end-to-end','R03 R25 R26 R28 R36 R40','Create an invoice, partially pay, finish paying and reconcile both receipts.', 'F0 billing staff and P;unique invoice responsibility64.50', 'Staff creates invoice. | Patient follows statement notification and previews bill. | Pay20.25, inspect partial balance and receipt. | Pay44.25, inspect final balance and second receipt. | Reopen Dashboard and history.', 'Ledger, UI, PDFs and notifications reconcile to64.50.', 'Exactly two transactions20.25/44.25. | Intermediate44.25 and final0.00 balances. | Two correct receipt PDFs. | Dashboard/notifications reflect changes. | Billing audit entries exist; no duplicate processing.')
case('Expert','Family access end-to-end','R30 R31 R32 R33 R34 R40','Complete scoped invitation, owner revocation and a new consent after revocation.', 'F0 adult P owner,Q proxy;no links', 'P invites Q results only. | Q accepts and views allowed result but cannot billing export. | P revokes. | Q retries old link/old invitation. | P sends a genuinely new invitation with visits only. | Q accepts and checks new scopes.', 'Revocation cannot be bypassed; only fresh consent establishes new access.', 'Old invite cannot restore access. | Fresh invitation requires new explicit acceptance. | New access permits visits only, not prior results/billing. | Proxy-change audit reflects grants/revocation accurately.')
case('Expert','Guardian verification','R31 R34 R35 R39 R40','Request dependent access, deny self-approval, then verify an administrator decision.', 'F0 minor D;requesterG;administrator;no grant', 'G requests guardian/dependent access. | Inspect pending state and attempt dependent record access. | Administrator tries decision without note, then enters synthetic verification and approves specific scopes. | G opens permitted dependent section. | Administrator revokes; G retries.', 'Guardian access is gated by recorded administrator verification.', 'No self-grant before decision. | Required verification note enforced. | Granted scopes honored; revocation denies next access. | Synthetic identity/guardian limitations disclosed. | Audit records decision and revocation.')
case('Expert','Account recovery end-to-end','R04 R05 R06 R07 R39','Recover access after a failed reset, then validate session/account isolation.', 'F0 P and Q;local mailbox;P authenticated in separate isolated browser profile;expired and valid reset fixtures', 'Attempt expired link then request valid recovery through UI. | Correct mismatch and complete reset from local mailbox. | Try old/new password. | Check already-open P authenticated page after refresh. | Sign out and sign in as Q without reload.', 'Recovery yields one valid new credential without stale cross-account access.', 'Expired/mismatched attempts do not alter password. | New credential works, old fails. | Existing sessions do not expose unauthorized post-reset content if invalidated; no cross-account leakage. | Q sees only Q data. | No external mail dependency.')
case('Expert','Care-team onboarding end-to-end','R08 R09 R14 R18 R21 R25 R39','Onboard all four permitted staff roles and verify their appropriate workspaces.', 'F0 administrator;four unused applicants with synthetic organizations', 'Register Physician, Nurse, Front Desk and Billing Staff separately. | Verify each pending restriction. | Administrator reviews each with verification note and approves. | Re-login each and perform one role-appropriate action: clinical reply, refill review, scheduling update, invoice creation.', 'Approved roles enter appropriate workspaces and execute authorized workflows.', 'All pending users denied staff records. | Four recorded approvals with notes. | Each final role equals approved role, not Administrator. | Role-appropriate changes persist and appear for relevant patient; no privilege from public selection alone.')
case('Expert','Audit and error recovery','R14 R17 R21 R25 R34 R38 R39 R40','Verify an audited cross-module staff session and recover from a missing record.', 'F0 authorized administrator and clinical/billing fixtures;read-only audit verifier enabled', 'Log in and open P record. | Update appointment, publish a result, edit medication, decide refill, change proxy permission and record simulated billing change. | Open supplied nonexistent record URL. | Use recovery navigation and reopen P.', 'Important events are auditable and missing-record errors do not strand the user.', 'Read-only audit inspection finds actor/time/target/action for login, access and all six mutations. | Error contains no internal model/query message and has usable return path. | P context and durable changes remain correct. | No real medical/payment operation.')

assert len(cases) == 100
assert {d:sum(c['difficulty']==d for c in cases) for d in ['Easy','Medium','Hard','Expert']} == {'Easy':30,'Medium':40,'Hard':20,'Expert':10}
assert len(set(c['task'] for c in cases)) == 100
for c in cases:
    assert all(r in requirements for r in c['requirement_ids'])
    assert c['expected_workflow'] and c['pass_fail_criteria']

if (ROOT/'freeze.json').exists():
    raise SystemExit('Suite already frozen. Do not overwrite; use a separately approved new evaluation if requirements change.')
spec_hash = hashlib.sha256(SPEC.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
suite = {'schema_version':1, 'description':{'path':'experiments/round-03/description.md','version':'3.0.0 / Round 3','sha256':spec_hash},
    'application_commit':BASE,'derivation':'Only the final consolidated Round 3 Description. Existing implementation/tests/results are not the expectation oracle.',
    'distribution':{'Easy':30,'Medium':40,'Hard':20,'Expert':10},'requirements':requirements,'tests':cases}
ROOT.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
(ROOT/'final_test_cases_100.json').write_text(json.dumps(suite,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
lines=['# Final V3 specification-based native CUA test suite','', 'Exactly 100 independent tests: Easy30 / Medium40 / Hard20 / Expert10.',
       '', 'Authority: `experiments/round-03/description.md` (3.0.0, Round3). No previous browser scores are reused.', '',
       'Each test resets to an independent synthetic baseline; no test depends on an earlier test passing. F0 and named fixture contracts are defined in `FIXTURES.md`. Runtime accounts/secrets and URLs are provided privately.',
       '', '## Requirement traceability','']
for rid,r in requirements.items(): lines.extend([f"- **{rid}** — {r['source_heading']}: {r['requirement']}"])
for level in suite['distribution']:
    lines.extend(['',f'## {level}',''])
    categories=list(dict.fromkeys(c['functional_category'] for c in cases if c['difficulty']==level))
    for category in categories:
        lines.extend([f'### {category}',''])
        for c in cases:
            if c['difficulty']!=level or c['functional_category']!=category: continue
            lines.extend([f"#### {c['id']} — {c['task']}",'',f"Requirements: {', '.join(c['requirement_ids'])}",'','Preconditions:'])
            lines.extend(f'- {p}' for p in c['preconditions'])
            lines.extend(['',f"Test data: {c['test_data']}",'','Expected workflow:',''])
            lines.extend(f'{i+1}. {s}' for i,s in enumerate(c['expected_workflow']))
            lines.extend(['',f"Expected result: {c['expected_result']}",'','Objective acceptance criteria:',''])
            lines.extend(f'- {s}' for s in c['pass_fail_criteria'])
            lines.extend(['',c['independent_verification'],''])
(ROOT/'FINAL_TEST_CASES.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines),encoding='utf-8')
print('Authored 100 unique tests; inspect and freeze before execution.')
